<title>FRANCE: Eurocopter says 1996 loss between 350-400 mln Ffr.</title>
<headline>Eurocopter says 1996 loss between 350-400 mln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eurocopter said on Monday it made a net consolidated loss of between 350 and 400 million francs in 1996 and abandoned plans to cut 300 jobs in 1998.</p>
<p>Eurcopter, a joint venture 70 percent owned by Aerospatiale and 30 percent by Daimler-Benz Aerospace, said reports in the press that it would make a loss of 450 million francs, including provisions of 100 million for 300 job cuts, were based on a worst case scenario.</p>
<p>It said the performance of Eurocopter during the past few months and the announcement on April 17 that the installation of tools to build the Tiger combat helicopter would start in June, led the management to abandon these plans.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
</text>
